    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51063.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "So let me ask you about the Senate that your playground for a while. Mitt Romney has come out and has decided that I'm done with this. I can't do this bullshitting anymore. I'm done. But on his way out has pretty much salted the earth or at least scorched it pretty damn good for Republicans in terms of what he sees happening inside the Senate that really kind of speaks to something that a number of us have been warning about for a while and that is the house is the leading edge of what's going to eventually wind up being part of the Senate as well, and that is this disintegration of norms and the institutional prerogatives, et cetera, for just crass politics. And he pretty much labeled that. You also have spoken to some of, again, going back to some of the cultural issues that sort of buffeted you at the time. about what was happening in some of these institutions. What's your take on what Mitt Romney said this week and how people are kind of responding to it?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_04",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
